  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance for Vulnerable Populations in the States of Amazonas, Apure, Bolivar, Delta Amacuro and Zulia in Venezuela</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will address urgent healthcare, mental health/psychosocial, and protection needs through an integrated and comprehensive approach. Additionally, the project will improve access to water, sanitation, and hygiene in vulnerable, indigenous communities and their local health facilities in the Venezuelan border states of Amazonas, Apure, Bol&#xed;var, and Zulia. Mobile teams comprising medical and psychosocial specialists conduct periodic visits to targeted communities to ensure the direct provision of quality, life-saving services. Concurrently, community health facilities are improved with the integration of infection prevention and control measures, the provision of disinfection kits, and the rehabilitation of WASH infrastructure in 19 centers. Additionally, primary healthcare professionals receive refresher training, while community health workers are trained in community-based disease surveillance, health promotion, and disease prevention. This training aims to enhance the health literacy of community members. All training activities are supported by mentorship throughout the implementation period. The MHPSS component is integrated with protection activities with the objective of promoting social cohesion and positive or neutral coping mechanisms, fostering group discussions of gender norms and protection risks, and reducing vulnerabilities to human trafficking, gender-based violence, and unsafe migration. Assistance is provided directly to survivors of violence and victims of trafficking, including safe accommodation, non-food items, and legal assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
